course: dictionary
lesson: 9913
title: Reading about tamarins
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Science books often use words you may not know yet, like tamarin. You can work out a lot from the words around it, and this is called context. Ask yourself what would make sense in the sentence.
explain: «Tamarins and marmosets usually have twins, and the father and older brothers and sisters carry the babies most of the time.» You may not know marmoset, but the sentence puts it beside tamarin, so it is probably a similar kind of animal.
explain: «Golden lion tamarins from Brazil fell to about 200 in the wild in the 1970s.» Fell here does not mean tumbled over. The number drops from many to about 200, so fell means dropped. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it.
fact: A tamarin is a small monkey from the rainforests of Central and South America.
fact: Tamarins have silky fur and a long tail.
fact: Some tamarins, like the golden lion tamarin, have a bright mane.
fact: Tamarins live in family groups, and the fathers often carry the babies.
fact: In the 1970s golden lion tamarins fell to about 200 in the wild, but zoos bred them and now there are a few thousand.
exercise: Where do tamarins live? | In deserts, far from any trees | In the cold mountains of Europe | *In the rainforests of Central and South America | In the seas near Australia
exercise: «Golden lion tamarins fell to about 200 in the wild.» What does fell mean here? | *Dropped in number | Tumbled over onto the ground | Climbed up high | Were born
exercise: «The father and older brothers and sisters carry the babies most of the time.» Who carries the babies? | Only the zoo keepers | A passing bird | Nobody, the babies walk alone | *The father, with older brothers and sisters
test: «Zoo-born animals may not know how to find food or avoid predators.» What is a predator? | *An animal that hunts other animals for food | A baby tamarin | A kind of zoo keeper | A tree that gives fruit
test: Which tamarin has a bright mane? | A baboon | *A golden lion tamarin | A sloth | A cotton-top tamarin
exam: In «Golden lion tamarins survived better once they were released in family groups», what does survived mean? | Got lost in the forest | Were sold to a zoo | *Lived on and stayed alive | Went to sleep
